@aojea It was not my intention to sound sarcastic or any of such sort! Rather I honestly think that @andrewsykim 's scenario is valid and we could make a generic improvement. 

Regarding the problem at hand, I believe that allowing control over the initial `NetworkUnavailable` condition on the kubelet is rather beneficial. With cloudprovider `external`, the kubelet would rather have a hard time with heuristics to determine what should be the initial condition settings, so delegate that to the cluster provider/owner. With something like that, your PR makes more sense (but would require some adaptations from `gce` users to their kubelet config).

Having said that, I understand that this is complex to navigate and not break things along. Thank you for looking into it.
